## 1. Key Architectural & Systems Discoveries

Inspection of `thinkingmachines/Inkling-2-Mini` (`config.json`) and `llama.cpp`'s `src/models/inkling2-loop.cpp` revealed four high-leverage optimization opportunities missed by default setups:

1. **Looped-Core-First GPU MoE Offloading (3× VRAM Leverage on 8 GB GPUs)**:
   - Inkling 2 Mini has **24 physical layers**, where physical layers `6..17` (12 core layers) execute **3 times per token** (`6 + 12×3 + 6 = 48` logical layers).
   - Standard `-ncmoe N` / `--n-cpu-moe N` offloads the *first N* physical layers (`0..N-1`), wasting VRAM on Prelude/Epilogue layers that run only **1× per token**.
   - By regex-pinning **only the looped core (`blk.6..13`)** to an 8 GB RTX 4060 Laptop GPU (`-ot "blk\.([0-5]|1[4-9]|2[0-3])\.ffn_.*_exps.=CPU"`) while keeping Prelude/Epilogue MoE experts on Ryzen AI 9 HX 370 AVX-512 CPU, every GiB of VRAM delivers **3× the compute leverage**:
     - Naive `--cpu-moe`: `pp512 = 274.9 tok/s`, `tg64 = 17.02 tok/s`
     - **Looped-Core-First (8 core layers = 24 logical passes on GPU)**: `pp512 = 372.46 tok/s (+35.5%)`, **`tg64 = 22.19 tok/s (+30.4%)`**!
   - For sustained live `llama-server` serving on Windows WDDM (8 GB VRAM), **two default traps cut live speed in half**:
     1. Default `-np 4` quadruples KV cache & compute buffers (`4 × 32K = 128K`), triggering silent Windows WDDM PCIe spill (`10.4 tok/s`). Setting **`-np 1 --load-mode none`** with **5 looped-core layers (`blk.6..10` = 15 logical passes)** stays strictly inside physical VRAM (`7,451 / 8,188 MiB`) for rock-solid **`18.8–20.6 tok/s`** sustained live decode (+97% over naive defaults).
     2. Enabling DSpark (`--spec-type draft-dspark`) on a hybrid GPU+CPU setup forces host-copy target feature transfers (`DFlash target features via host copies`) and CPU draft verification, dropping live decode from `20.57 tok/s` to `10.49 tok/s` despite a `50.7%` draft acceptance rate.

2. **Why 256K Context Fits Easily on 64 GB Strix Point (`8 Global + 40 SWA-1024`)**:
   - Out of 24 physical layers, **20 use 1,024-token Sliding Window Attention (SWA)** and only **4 physical layers (`5, 11, 17, 23`) use Global Full Attention**.
   - Across the 3 core passes, **only 8 out of 48 logical layers** (`5, 11, 17, 23, 29, 35, 41, 47`) retain full-context KV cache (`8 KV heads × 128 dim × 2 (K+V) = 16 KB/token` at `Q8_0`), while the other 40 logical layers are capped at a fixed `~160 MB` total!
   - Result on **Fedora 45 (Ryzen AI 9 HX 370 + Radeon 890M `gfx1150`, 64 GB Unified Memory)**:
     - **262,144 (256K) context** + `UD-Q4_K_XL` (16.41 GiB) + `mmproj-F16.gguf` (vision) + Pass-2/3 control vector loads in **`3.48 s`** with **`28 GiB RAM still free`**!
     - **Vulkan RADV STRIX1 (`8.16–8.48 tok/s`) outperforms ROCm `gfx1150` (`5.10 tok/s`) by +60–66%** on decode, and outperforms **Qwen 3.8 27B Dense (`4.77 tok/s`) by +78%** on the exact same machine!

3. **World-First Pass-Targeted Inner-Loop Steering (Layers `24..47` Only)**:
   - Because `llama.cpp` expands Inkling 2 Mini's 24 physical layers into **48 distinct logical slots** (`0..5` Prelude, `6..17` Pass 1, `18..23` Epilogue, `24..35` Pass 2, `36..47` Pass 3), GGUF control vectors (`--control-vector`) can target **Pass 2 & Pass 3 exclusively (`--control-vector-layer-range 24 47`)**!
   - This leaves Pass 1 comprehension and Epilogue syntax 100% untouched while steering the cross-pass iterative refinement loops toward Glacier C#/.NET 10 zero-alloc SIMD/GPU invariants and epistemic honesty.
   - Extracted via contrastive SVD in Inkling 2 Mini's native 2,304-dim representation space (`contrastive_separation = 0.3736`), saved to `adapters/glacier_pass23_cvec.gguf`.

4. **Outer Research-Injection + Context-Compaction Loop (`research_loop_proxy.py`)**:
   - OpenAI-compatible proxy (`:8090`) that indexes the local repository (`2,711` files), retrieves keyword-windowed file/symbol evidence (and explicit *verified negative results* when an API does not exist!) in **`9.3 ms`**, optionally queries `Glacier.Oracle` for live web grounding, preserves a byte-identical static system prefix for ~100% KV prompt-cache reuse, compacts older middle turns to protect KV budget, and routes Inkling 2 Mini's native `reasoning_effort` (`0.2` / `0.7` / `0.9` / `0.99`).

